      "problem": "$\\frac{4{x}^{4}+12{x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}+16x+7}{x+3}=$",
      "worked_solution": "We can calculate $\\frac{4{x}^{4}+12{x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}+16x+7}{x+3}$ using synthetic division.\n\nCarrying out the synthetic division process, we arrive at the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {x}^{4} & {x}^{3} & {x}^{2} & {x}^{1} & {x}^{0} \\\\ -3 & 4 & 12 & 5 & 16 & 7 \\\\  & ↓ & -12 & 0 & -15 & -3 \\\\  & 4 & 0 & 5 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4{x}^{4}+12{x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}+16x+7}{x+3}=4{x}^{3}+5x+1+\\frac{4}{x+3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
