      "problem": "$\\frac{-{x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+x+1}{x+4}=$",
      "worked_solution": "We can calculate $\\frac{-{x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+x+1}{x+4}$ using synthetic division.\n\nCarrying out the synthetic division process, we arrive at the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {x}^{4} & {x}^{3} & {x}^{2} & {x}^{1} & {x}^{0} \\\\ -4 & -1 & -3 & 4 & 1 & 1 \\\\  & ↓ & 4 & -4 & 0 & -4 \\\\  & -1 & 1 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-{x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+x+1}{x+4}=-{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+1-\\frac{3}{x+4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
